# Deploy commands for the user

When the user must run something on the server (Termius, SSH, `/opt/aiapp`), give **one** copy-paste line. Chain with `&&`. Do not split into a multi-line script, a numbered list of commands, or several fenced blocks.

Example: `cd /opt/aiapp && git pull origin main && make prod-frontend`

Keep comments and explanations outside that line. If a secret is required, put the assignment in the same line (`WP_ADMIN_PASSWORD='…' bash scripts/wp-bootstrap.sh`). Stop after a failed step is implied by `&&`.

This applies only to commands the user runs. Agent-executed local git/tests stay as tool calls.
